1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:04,146
Here is how a new Australian
fund becomes a token

2
00:00:04,146 --> 00:00:07,696
on Redbelly Network, through
Tokeniser, in 4 stages.

3
00:00:08,296 --> 00:00:11,219
Tokenisation records
ownership as digital tokens,

4
00:00:11,219 --> 00:00:13,843
and lets you program
the rules of the asset.

5
00:00:14,443 --> 00:00:16,460
Stage 1, legal preparation.

6
00:00:16,710 --> 00:00:20,839
The fund's documents must allow
ownership to be recorded on a blockchain.

7
00:00:21,089 --> 00:00:24,728
No separate tokenisation
licence is needed in Australia.

8
00:00:25,328 --> 00:00:27,230
Stage 2, platform onboarding.

9
00:00:27,480 --> 00:00:32,137
The manager and the fund are verified
on Tokeniser, and the token is designed.

10
00:00:32,737 --> 00:00:35,221
Stage 3, compliance configuration.

11
00:00:35,471 --> 00:00:38,598
Identity checks, who may
invest, and transfer limits

12
00:00:38,598 --> 00:00:41,846
are encoded into the token
and enforced automatically.

13
00:00:42,446 --> 00:00:44,583
Stage 4, the investor register.

14
00:00:44,833 --> 00:00:48,775
Each investor verifies their
identity and gets a digital wallet.

15
00:00:49,025 --> 00:00:51,023
No tokens are issued until then.

16
00:00:51,623 --> 00:00:55,874
Tokens are then issued on Redbelly
Network, into verified wallets.

17
00:00:56,124 --> 00:01:00,191
From the first token, this register
is the official record of ownership.

18
00:01:00,791 --> 00:01:05,017
Every transfer is checked against the
rules first, and breaches are rejected.

19
00:01:05,267 --> 00:01:07,376
When investors hold their own wallet,

20
00:01:07,376 --> 00:01:10,282
transfer and payment complete
together, in seconds.

21
00:01:10,882 --> 00:01:15,586
Tokeniser operates on Redbelly Network,
Australia's public digital token

22
00:01:15,586 --> 00:01:20,617
infrastructure, where transactions are
confirmed once and cannot be reversed.
